# Pinned mybigday/llama.rn revision that produced the vendored rn-* glue in
# llama-kt/src/main/cpp/ and the inherited patches in scripts/patches/.
#
# v0.12.6 — https://github.com/mybigday/llama.rn/releases/tag/v0.12.6
# (annotated tag object 84ccc527; this is the commit it points to)
#
# Coupled with third_party/llama.cpp: llama.rn v0.12.6 pins llama.cpp at
# 99f3dc32296f825fec94f202da1e9fede1e78cf9, the same commit as our submodule.
# The inherited patches are written against that llama.cpp, so the two move
# together (TEN-87). bootstrap.sh copies the rn-* files verbatim (the LM_
# rewrite explicitly skips rn-*); the three targets of patches/0002 are the only
# ones that differ from this commit's cpp/ tree.
#
# To bump: pick the new llama.rn revision, put its full sha here, move the
# llama.cpp submodule to the sha that revision pins, re-run bootstrap.sh, and
# re-port patches/0002 if the rn-completion/rn-llama hunks moved.
